**Key Pareto-front candidates:**
- **14-0add-8deg (run2)**: 189 bar / 0.71 — clean membrane, good balance
- **14p8-17deg (run2)**: 217 bar / 0.82 — highest pore fraction observed, but has wrinkles; only 1 run
- **15-8deg**: 253 bar / 0.69 — wrinkle present, only 1 run

The **14p8-17deg (run2)** result (polymer_wt=14.8, bath_temp=17, pullcast_speed=17, mixing_temp=72, coupon_to_bath_wait_time=530, nips_bath_wait_time=1425, N2=true) shows the highest pore fraction (0.82) with a respectable modulus (217 bar). This is a large apparent gain over anything else in the dataset. However:
