**Rationale:** This experiment targets an under-sampled region combining the high-pore-fraction tendency of lower polymer concentrations (~14–15 wt%) with a bath temperature (10°C) that sits between the 8°C region (high pore fraction, moderate modulus) and the 13°C region (higher modulus). The moderate pullcast speed (7 mm/s) and N2 atmosphere aim to reduce the wrinkle defects seen at higher speeds. The mixing temperature of 45°C ensures proper dissolution of the 14.5 wt% solution. If successful, this could advance the Pareto front by achieving both higher pore fraction (>0.65) and respectable modulus (>200 bar) in a clean membrane. It also fills a genuine gap in the bath_temp × polymer_wt space.

